L e g i o n a r y
________________
[ C h a m p i o n ] ~ [ B r e a c h e r ] ~ [ F o r m a t i o n ]
________________
He was not just another cog in the machine. His will and his might would change this broken world. Equipped with the latest and best equipment Eterion had to offer, he would tame the unreality with his virtuous comrades. His blade had been sharpened for hours. His armour shone like a bright, silvery gemstone. His shield concealed a tiny cannon, the pride and joy of his homeland’s military engineers. All of his bravado would fade at the sight of his own blood soaking an enemy’s crude, serrated implement.


She had spent enough time in this place to understand its calculus. The ore had to reach the port in two days, passing through a famously lethal mountain pass, then through an active warzone only to end up in cannibal infested woodlands. The price of ore is well known, as is the price of a soul. She added up the costs and assigned the indebted men and women to their duties, those more experienced to the transport, those less fortunate to “protection” squads. She thought this exchange rational, thinking she would feel at peace with her own duty when it was time for her to do the same.


They stood shoulder to shoulder, inseparable since childhood. They had the entire song and dance down to a science. A shieldbearer in the front, a gunman to take out those who would sabotage their little formation in the back and two warriors to the sides, mowing down whatever got caught on their long blades. A moment of distraction was all it took for the firebomb to hit them, for the gunman to be set ablaze. With all of the grace and delirium of an amputee, they would march on like usual, holding on to their crushed souls, as if that would bring him back from the ashes.
________________


Legionaries are trained and versatile servants. They perform a variety of duties ranging from warfare to construction and logistics, serving as the backbone of any modern task force. Some specialize in close quarters combat, others prefer ranged weapons, what binds them are the creative ways in which they outplay their opponents. No matter their origin or style, legionaries are industrious combat engineers disciplined enough to achieve any task, given enough resources or souls.
________________


Recommended disciplines: Warfare/Duel, Leadership
Recommended special skills: Carry, Engineering, Stance, Scout
