The patrons’ voices grew ever louder, turning from cheers into a heated debate. Music soon stopped and only the drunken yells could be heard throughout the establishment. A menacing figure pushed through the crowd to stand before the instigator, measuring him up in silence. The instigator apologized, sat down, and the brawl was postponed to a later date.


The novice desperately tried to hold off the approaching branches with his spear as his allies’ breathless bodies hung strung above him. As one took hold of him, just as swiftly was it chopped off by a powerful swing of an axe. A hulking, metal figure grabbed the novice, pulling him through the thick bushes from which she came. The novice pleaded with her to return for his comrades, yet she would not allow herself to feel sorry. That novice was not the first nor the last one she would have to drag out of hell that night


As he stood behind his lord listening to his speech, his mind wandered to his childhood. He recalled standing on a similar podium, tiny and scared, watching his mother be brought to the gallows. The lord still spoke in a similar manner, high and mighty, though his voice was much less intimidating coming from his present hunched, frail form. Armored from head to toe, he walked up to the lord and squeezed him by the neck. While he knew that he would be struck down, he was sure that his loyal shell would let him finish this final task with entire seconds to spare.
________________


Wardens are heavily armored fighters serving as the frontline of any force they are a part of. Often trained in more diplomatic approaches, their aim is to prevent conflict first and defend second. If their menacing presence doesn’t defuse the situation by itself, their prowess and brutality eventually will.
