As the feast was nearing its end, she arose from her seat, an old flimsy rapier on her hip, and issued a challenge for the rank to her commanding officer. He snickered among his close associates, calling on his armored warden to duel in his stead. She engaged the iron golem in a mockery of a fencing match, making provocative yet harmless strikes at his iron shell. When the golem decided to end the duel by simply coming at her, she made a final feint, snapped open his visor and shot him with a gun concealed within her sleeve. While she may have been shaken, her body would never betray her by showing it to the silent crowd.


He had been sent to quell a peasant uprising in the borderlands. His trained men had made quick work of the rabble. Descending upon the rebels’ last stronghold, they would be greeted not by desperate resistance, but a single, disheveled man, offering to resolve the issue with only a single death. They agreed on the terms - immediate surrender or mercy for the rebels. His shiny engraved saber had crossed with many blades, yet never had it met a piece of iron as crude and frail as his opponent’s rusty sword. In but a few swings he had cut off the rebel leader’s hand, yet the sight of his surrendered body kneeling in the mud stopped his arm from performing the final swing. Without a single word, he would turn back and order his men to depart the hamlet.


When she woke up her rival’s mercenaries had already begun torching the manor. She would usher her children and servants through the secret passage, shoving various heirlooms into their shaking hands. By the time they were all safe her muscles were tired and her throat burned. Coughing, half dressed and a molten blade in hand, she had emerged through the front entrance and waved a challenge to her murderers. They had to see her go down if her children were to ever live in peace. Her broken, charred body would display all of her life’s achievements to a dozen of them before it finally ran out of adrenaline. In her final moments, she laid down her blade and kneeled before her decapitators, taking one final look at the stars.
________________


Duelists are skilled and elegant fighters who specialize in single combat. Unlike the more savage warriors of the world, they are more akin to entertainers, putting on a good show in addition to slaying their foe. They prefer one handed weapons paired with either a parrying tool or a sidearm, utilizing a complex combat technique in order to gain advantage. Their form is perfect and their reflexes sharp - no trick will surprise them.
