He stood upon the stage, the festival crowd below him, humming along to his melody. They did not know it, but this night would stay with them forever. After a brief pause, he inserted an ambedic crystal into his modified violin, a shard containing the happiest of memories he had shared with his late wife. Though he played a familiar love song, his reproduction gave it a surreal texture as the shard emitted its contents to those who bore witness. The song, a well-known common vessel, had been applied magnificently to instill the most human of memories within the audience.


She was the first person they would turn to whenever they would encounter even a slight obstacle. She did not simply reproduce legendary music, she warped it beyond recognition into the specific, unique form for every situation that required it. Her songs turned cowards and lowlives into determined, unstoppable machines with naught but sound and emotion. Her melodies pushed individual heroes to their absolute limits. Her delusional, assuring lyrics lured them to their deaths at the hands of an enemy no sane person would have confronted. Their loss was no matter, though, as she could always record their own final moments and twist them to inspire her next band.


He was beyond conviction and beyond care. He was left all alone, and his supply of blood was rapidly running out. He prepared his instrument for the final performance, connecting directly to its ambedic mechanism. The almost silent melody grew in strength as they peppered him with arrows. At first the sound was just grating, a minor inconvenience. When he started deliriously singing, blood bubbling in his mouth, his audience was hit by countless invisible slashes, reflecting his wounds upon them. When he finally collapsed, the song continued to escalate into an incomprehensible cacophony, turning his murderers into a writhing funeral pyre.
________________


Bards are artists and amplifiers of emotion. They utilize instruments modified to host ambedic crystals, turning their performances from simple music to powerful psychological auras. Bards inspire their allies beyond anything commonly possible, and they stunt their enemies in ways they can hardly comprehend. This shaping and warping of known songs taps into the powers of the seasons without conviction, relying instead on pure emotion and memory to fuel the process.
________________


