As he was being transported to the scene they briefed him on the situation, on the trapped family and the maniac who was about to burn down the building they were in. Before entering his assistant passed him a tiny pistol which he tucked away in his pocket. Entering the building, he could see naught but dim, dusty hallways and narrow passages. He pleaded with the beast for nearly an hour before finally snapping at the gruesome plan the beast had presented concerning the little girl. He initiated the brawl with the intent to deceive, and when the beast got tired and pulled out a knife he placed a single precise shot in its dome. This was the last time he would agree to participate in such a negotiation.


He knew they were after him for a long while. There was no easy way to purge the force of the traitors, so his best idea was to set a trap. He organized every detail of the ambush himself, he set his allies up in the exact positions and gave them a precise timeline. He had thought of everything, and all that was left was to convince his opponents he had not. He placed himself into an exposed office with a single entryway and waited. When they found him he could barely even strike at them before they knocked him to the ground, stabbed him in the back and shot his hands. His allies would reach them in time and capture them for memory extraction, yet his body would forever bear the scars of his master plan.


She looked solemnly over the battlefield-to-become, despairing at the little hope they had left. They had lost too many men already, and the upcoming battle was about to become the final nail in their collective coffin. In what might have been an erratic and delusional idea, she donned her old armour and marched herself to the frontlines below. She had led them into death for too long, and if she was to do so again she could not bear witness. She would be the one to lead them into doom, and if luck allowed it, she would give them the tiniest of surges before fading into nothingness. As she made her way to the line of death, she had one last conversation with each of her close friends, those who had given her their all. Standing on the final rampart, she would prepare her rhetoric routine for the final time, producing a form-perfect rallying speech before descending into the mayhem. When she was impaled, she mustered everything she had to give them a final, frozen smile.
________________


Envoys are diplomats and commanders well versed in negotiation tactics and leadership roles. They prefer to attempt a conversation before resorting to more primitive means of conflict resolution. While some envoys prefer to lead from the front and amongst their allies, others work best within the confines of their own minds and the safety of the backlines, driving their allies to perform unimaginable feats through rhetoric and poetry.
