It finally moved! She had been working on the little automaton for months, and she finally managed to get it to move. She was starting to get frustrated, not knowing whether it was the design of the motor and the legs or her ambedic link to the little machine that was at fault. For someone who was proud to exclaim that she would never mother a child, she sure seemed excited to witness her creation shift and shake, even if it ultimately was just a cold construct.


He sat behind tall cover, a blindfold over his eyes. He used the first construct to plant a breach charge on the enemy’s wall. Once it blew open, the second construct flew into the building, equipped with a flamethrower and an oil spewing mechanism. Luckily, he had recently installed a transmission dampener onto his ambedic receiver in order to block out unnecessary emotions and increase his efficiency at piloting such a horrifying machine. After a few rounds of drinks, he was even able to forget the face of the child that was inside the building.


She stood inside her construct-suit, placed in between the firing line and the wounded civilians behind her. Before charging into the gunmen she recalled how sad she felt when she disassembled her old construct so she could use its battery to power this monstrous suit. As the bullets rained upon her firm but still destructible shell, she could swear she heard it thank her.
________________


Mechanists are pioneers of robotics, assembling and piloting the very first of such creations. They combine their knowledge of mechanics and ambedic technology in order to create remotely-controllable extensions of their body in the form of robotic companions. Due to the great mental load operating such a construct demands, the very best of the mechanists can only ever optimally operate two smaller constructs or a single more complex one at any given moment.
