After a battle would end, she would arrive. To tend to the survivors’ wounds, but more importantly to their souls. No matter the side, no matter the goal, no matter the thanks, she would comfort each and every living and dying soul, easing their mental toll and letting them return to their regular lives. She would take in all of this pain and dissolve it within herself, becoming a tiny bit more hollow each time, becoming a tiny bit more capable each time, becoming a tiny bit more nobody each time.


He knew of both the dangers and boons of the planar edge. He’d spent his life studying it, wandering the void in between, in search of things forgotten and things yet to be learned. By the time they accused him of dark magic he was already long gone from the town. By the time the brigands shot at him he was already prepared to dodge each and every arrow sent his way in an arrangement of movements no human could ever attempt. By the time the axe split his head, he had already long made peace with his inevitable fate.


Armed with naught but a walking stick, she barged into the target’s house. The coward tried to ambush her, yet his arms flickered and his sword fell through them to the ground. “Did you murder them?” - she asked in an unfeeling tone. Before the accused could even open his mouth, his mind had already betrayed him, spilling out all that went through it. Satisfied with the answer, she declared her judgement. The coward’s body slumped to the ground, his mind detaching from the person, aimlessly staring at the floor. In but a minute the coward would flicker away for the last time, disappearing not just from reality but from the minds of those who knew him. She never felt bad about what she had to do, in part because she thought oblivion preferable to corporeal punishment, in part because her memory of them would soon expire.
________________


Empaths are diviners and telepaths capable of previewing the thoughts and emotions of living creatures as well as severely dampening them. Some empaths fully dedicate themselves to interpretation of creatures and are able to predict their actions in advance while others prefer to hone their ability to disrupt the stream of consciousness, becoming capable of fully erasing living beings from existence. While these abilities are powerful, empaths are often limited in their use due to their devotion to the ideals of Bruma, making them possibly the least destructive type of mystic.
