His parents woke him and his sister up in the middle of the night in a panicked hurry. They barely had time to dress before they were dragged out of their house and into the dark woods, alone. As they ran they could hear screams behind them and see a pyre where their home once stood. After hours of travel they collapsed in a secluded den, holding hands as they shook from the cold. He berated himself for not bringing a lighter, matches, anything to keep the cold at bay. At some point during the night their hands lit ablaze.


When they woke up in the forest with their oil and torches gone they thought they wouldn’t last a day longer. Their scorchblades could provide them some light, yes, but not enough to weather the endless nights. It was precisely in the moment where they stood surrounded with cold, burnt out blades in their hands that she ignited. She would give her flesh to be their beacon in the final stand. As fire spread throughout her, their blades ignited once more and even began to spew fire on the beasts assaulting them. The miracle of her charred flesh gave them time, but more importantly it gave them hope. What remained of her body was brought back to the city and placed in a casket on a public square where she would forever watch over the central pyre.


Throughout the night he stood on the castle tower bombarding the battlements below with fire fueled by his flesh. The sparks flew and jumped as if they had a will of their own, spreading through the enemy forces almost like a bolt of lightning. Throughout the night he saw many of his friends fall and the parts of the various halls he walked now bloodied and ravaged. Throughout the night he treated his flesh and did all in his power to stop it from fully burning out, yet his body was nearing its limit. The final nail was not that he lacked the will to die for the cause or that he had no body left to burn. The final blow was the realization that his sacrifice here never even mattered, that no matter his power he would never have been able to protect them. His fire was finally snuffed out, and his half intact body collapsed on the floor, not sure what to even think about in its final moments.
________________


Sorcerers are powerful channelers of flame capable of igniting their flesh and controlling the fire this produces. They excel at ravaging hordes of fleshy beings, though with more precision they can also act as supportive leaders who provide their allies with lit weaponry, cauterize their wounds as they appear and light the paths they walk. All of this is paid for in full by their bodies as their flesh degrades from repeated burns, leaving them marked by their devotion to Vamor.
