She burst into the dimly lit cellar with only a purple flower in hand. On a central table there was a beggar, his leg amputated in order to evoke more pity from the passersby. Around him, two grotesque figures stood, instruments of pain in hand and grimaces in place of what would be their faces. She took a whiff of the flower and attuned to the torturer’s bodies, analysing their bones and muscles. Seconds later, they would fall to the ground, puke erupting from their orifices, blood trickling from their flayed skin. All that was left to restore the balance was to mend the beggar’s appendage back where it belonged.


The winter after her husband’s death had almost killed her. Isolated in that forest, she could barely sustain herself on berries and the pitiful produce of her garden. In desperation, she turned to her late husband’s study in search of a solution. While she was shocked to learn of the true nature of his research, it would prove to be her salvation. She exhumed his corpse and raised a revenant of flesh, just like his journal had explained. With tears in her eyes and peace in her heart, she would order “it” to hunt.


They all hated him and they all relied on him to survive. He began to wonder if his presence had made his comrades’ instincts duller, their recklessness worse. They would break formation to assault beasts head on, knowing he would quickly reattach any appendage or organ they lost. They charged into fire fully expecting him to regrow their skin once the dust had settled. He was a useful freak, a monster capable of unmaking or remaking life, but a freak they could no longer function without.
________________


Witches are occult healers and mediums versed in the arts of fleshweaving and necromancy. Some witches place a greater importance on manipulation of flesh and the living, acting as potent grafters or inflicting great harm upon skin and bone. Other witches work to perfect their mastery and control over the dead, being able to temporarily or permanently recall souls into their decaying bodies and bend their actions to their will. Due to their devotion to Halice, witches are often radical individuals bent on shaping the world into a new form. Even the corpses of those who opposed them will rise again to serve those ideals.
________________
Recommended disciplines: Zeal/Mysticism
Recommended specializations: Whisper, Medicine, Lore, Discipline


Class Features:
                  * Rhythm of Life
Passive
Requires: Witch Rank 0
Effect:
When performing a Survival or Medicine check on a creature, you may gain Strain to increase your result by that much up to a maximum of +2.
Halice abilities that require Attunement can be performed without it and apply it to their targets after being performed.
                  *   >>   Fleshbound Hex
Utility
Requires: Witch Rank 1
| 4 SN |
Effect:
Target up to 3 targets within your Attunement network, remove them from the network and inflict one of the following upon them:
Flay Skin: Inflict Bleeding 2.
Grind Bones: Inflict Stun 2. The target cannot move until the end of their next turn (CL 18 Stance save).
Spoil Humors: Inflict Feeble 2. The target suffers +1 DMG from all sources until the end of your next turn.
                  *   >>   Emergency Binding
Defensive
Requires: Witch Rank 2
Conviction: Halice
| 4 SN | +1 EVA |
Effect:
Target yourself or an ally. The target restores VG equal to the VG they lost since their previous turn +1. Each consecutive use of this ability also inflicts Bleeding equal to the number of times the ability has been used.


