CH VII. Aspects
Aspects are specific internalized mechanisms, narratives and trains of thought present within Reverie’s characters. They are most often adopted as the character interacts with the world and builds specific habits which cement into predictable and useful behaviors. Most aspects tend to feature an active component, some kind of task or mini-challenge that will provide a reward when the character completes it, creating additional things to do and strive towards in non-combat situations. A smaller number of Aspects also serves to provide a tangible combat benefit, but as all other aspects this too comes with a drawback.


Aspect slots are earned through advancements and aspects they may be adopted at any point at the cost of spending a DP maximum if the requirements are met. 


Aspects are loosely split between 8 categories:
                        * Grit - concerning physicality and how it impacts daily life
                        * Reflex - concerning attentiveness and how it impacts daily life
                        * Intellect - concerning thought and how it impacts daily life
                        * Psyche - concerning social competence and how it impacts daily life
                        * Comfort - concerning items and equipment and their expanded use
                        * Tactics - concerning temporary destiny points gained in combat
                        * Virtue - concerning enhanced displays of seasonal devotion
                        * Degradation - concerning adaptations to life with permanent failings


Only a single tactics aspect may trigger per combat encounter.
________________


Grit Aspects
	Requirements
	Body For Sale
A blow for a drink! Three hard smacks for a hearty meal! Your body is a ravaged battlefield bearing countless scars. While phantom pain still sometimes manifests, you've built up a considerable amount of tolerance to physical force and exhaustion.


[+] Exerting GRT checks costs 2 Strain less
[-] Failing GRT checks inflicts 2 DMG
	• GRT 1
• have been injured 3 times
	Weight of The World
There was a point in time where you packed your backpack full of things you might need on some journey or trip, and you've been reluctant to empty it ever since. It weighs a bit, sure, but wouldn't it be so embarrassing to be caught unprepared? The longer this went on the more you had to justify it - you're not just making sure you are ready for anything, you are the one bearing the entire weight of the world on your shoulders, refusing to let it ever catch you off guard. Someday, you might even find a use for some of the junk you're carrying.


[+] Gain 5 Burden capacity
[-] Suffer +1 SN from all sources while having 3 or more unused Burden
	• GRT 1
• spend two weeks being overburdened
	Righteous Punching Bag
Feeling it can be easy to get lost in the matters of morality, you've developed an escape hatch for this crisis - in a moment of desperation you shut off all thought and become a truly immovable righteous punching bag. Getting assaulted over and over by both man and object hurts, but at least it hurts less than being tormented by your opinionated soul. After all, there's no way you could do something wrong by protecting your allies and ideals, right?


[+] Whenever you suffer DMG from an action where you are defending your conviction or an ally, heal 3 Strain
[-] If you would suffer a crisis after receiving DMG, you suffer another crisis
	• GRT 1
• have defended a conviction which resulted in combat
	Warlock of Adrenal Lines
You have made a pact with your flesh and its soul. These "adrenal lines" have allowed you to call upon them to ignore all punishment in your time of need. This debt will be repaid by your pain receptors when you wake up the morning after.


[+] You may exert rolls while injured, and in doing so ignore the injury penalty for that roll
[-] Exerting rolls while bearing a relevant injury increases the healing time by a week
	• GRT 2
• have spent 2 weeks doing something instead of healing
	________________




Grit Aspects
	Requirements
	Emotional Meatshield
You have decided to better your physique as a form of character growth journey, and have managed to tie a lot of your self worth into the routine, willpower and effort you put into growing a big and strong body. This has made you impressively resolute, yet you constantly worry that something could end up preventing you from maintaining your body and erase months of progress.


[+] You may use the Discipline skill instead of Willpower and suffer VG instead of SN if you have reached your SL
[-] You must spend at least a week on physical training each month or suffer a crisis


	• GRT 2
• spend destiny points on skill checks or combat rolls while at your DP max 3 times
	

	• GRT 2
•
	Avatar of Violent Defiance
Your vision blurs and the pain stops. Your gut has been pierced by a spear, your back peppered with arrows, your eye shot out. Your entire existence is reduced to nothing but a single goal, a single perspective of view. NOTHING will make you fall for as long as you remain human.


[+] You may ignore the death rolls of damage instances you receive while on Death's Door by suffering 3 crises for as long as you can pay their costs.
[-] Doing this inflicts 2 SN upon your allies.
	• GRT 3
• survive a blow on death's door
	

	• GRT 3
•
