Reflex Aspects
	Requirements
	Internal Sensory Bleed
Something in your head clicked and ever since you've been one with your surroundings. You are "in sync" with reality and you navigate the world with exceptional ease, almost as if a semipermeable membrane allowed you to absorb its signals intrinsically. While this feels like a superpower, the occasional lapse of judgement can often lead to this membrane breaking, overwhelming your senses entirely.


[+] Exerting REF checks costs 2 Strain less
[-] Failing REF checks inflicts 2 DMG
	• REF 1
• have rolled an 18 on any 3d6 roll
	Shadow on The Wall
A cruel upbringing has taught you that it's often better to remain in the background, trying to avoid sticking out as much as possible. You've done it for so long it's become effortless, an instinctive way to exist. It can be very advantageous to be able to unexpectedly enter situations, yet a voice in the back of your head won't stop reminding you of the punishment you were given for sticking out in the past.


[+] You are not noticed by people who aren't specifically looking for you
[-] Being detected by non-allies inflicts you with 4 SN
	• REF 1
• participate in 3 significant scenes without exiting stealth
	Vain Construct Pilot
Moving elegantly is the universal standard you set for yourself. Appearing clumsy and failing to perform a bodily movement are actions you are disgusted by more than is probably healthy. You like showing off your masterful control over your vessel in minute triumphs, specific impressive movements, and if you fail to execute them you relive that failure for months every time you get a moment of quiet


[+] When performing physical skill checks, you may declare an intended target result. If you succeed the check and meet the result, you gain a temporary destiny point that lasts until the end of the session.
[-] You suffer a crisis if you fail to meet the target result.
	• REF 1
• exert already successful rolls 3 times
	Decree of The Gut
Your brain has noticed that a significant portion of the population seems to suffer from a condition known as "having integrity". You admire this trait, but have concluded that it could end up leading you into problems that could have been more easily avoided had you just trusted your gut. Are you really a horrible person if you occasionally go against your belief system? Your gut believes that these exceptions prove the rules.


[+] You may spend half of your DP maximum, rounded up to avoid a crisis from defying convictions.
[-] The bonus modifier to rolls aligning with your convictions is reduced by 1
	• REF 2
• defy your convictions 3 times
	________________




Reflex Aspects
	Requirements
	Irrelevant Detail Diviner
You are obsessed with watching your surroundings. Despite all reason, you are convinced you are one day going to notice some obscure detail that turns your life around and solves all of your problems. You're of the opinion that good senses mean little if they are wasted on someone who only occasionally remembers to use them.


[+] Take note whenever you succeed on a Perception check. When this count reaches your DP maximum, gain a Destiny Point.
[-] Failing a Perception check inflicts 4 Strain and resets the progress of this aspect
