Intellect Aspects
	Requirements
	Anti-Impostor Protocol
You are on a quest to learn all there is to know, and you will push yourself hard to unravel the situations you are placed in. Despite this, intellectual humiliation remains your one true fear sending you into a spiral upon even the slightest of failures.


[+] Exerting INT checks costs 2 Strain less
[-] Failing INT checks inflicts 2 Strain
	• INT 1
• have exerted 3 skill checks where you've had at least a +3 modifier
	Prisoner of Restless Nights
Everyone has those nights where they turn in their bed, cringing at an embarrassing moment or a difficult dilemma. You have had so many of them you have gained the ability to regain your composure and critically analyze what went wrong and where. Every one of your days ends in a determined self-promise to repent for your mistakes before you finally turn the pillow over to the cold side and fall asleep.


[+] You gain +1 modifier for skill checks for each attempt to complete them beyond the first once per week
[-] You suffer a 1 SN reduction towards your SL per attempt until you complete the skill check or give up and forfeit the modifier
	• INT 1
• fail the same check three times
	Dictator of Possible Outcomes
Nothing feels better to you than waking up and mapping out a plan of attack for the day. Vision and certainty are something you value above all else and you do your best to always radiate them. When you declare that a task needs doing, done it shall be! Failing to do so would bring great shame and dishonor not just to you but to everything you ever stood for.


[+] At the start of a day you may declare your intent to complete a task gain a single free exert on a check that contributes towards it
[-] Failing this task inflicts you with a crisis
	• INT 1
• declare intent to complete a task and then do so 3 times without fail
	Conveniently Prepared Thing
You once found an oddly shaped rock and lugged it around with you wherever you went for months. When someone finally asked "Does anyone have an oddly shaped rock?" this quirk grew into an obsession. You now consistently dedicate a pocket on your person to randomly selected items you have decided could come in useful some day and revel in the looks others give you when you conveniently show off the weird object you had on you've carried for unnaturally long stretches of time.


[+] Once per day, you may retroactively declare you have any regular you own or could have easily obtained.
[-] Your Burden capacity is reduced by 2
	• INT 2
• find a use for an item you chose to carry around without an obvious use case
	________________




Psyche Aspects
	Requirements
	Socially Powered Animal
You live to socialize and interact with your fellows, and have gotten pretty good at doing so over the countless hours of debating fools. Your willpower to endure these encounters is impressive, though your efforts can occasionally leave you enthralled by pointless arguments.


[+] Exerting PSY checks costs 2 Strain less
[-] Failing PSY checks inflicts 2 Strain
	• PSY 1
• have participated in 3 negotiations
	Keeper of Others' Woes
Your willingness to listen to people complaining has turned you into your social circle's dedicated amateur psychologist. You initially thought that it wasn't a big deal, but over time they have begun asking you questions like "What should I do about this?" that have made you reconsider your politeness. You still try to help and even enjoy doing so, but to say it wasn't more than you bargained for would be an utter lie.


[+] You may prevent others from suffering a crisis by paying 2 destiny points
[-] When doing this, roll 1d6 and suffer a crisis yourself if you roll 3 or below
	• PSY 1
• have witnessed an ally gain and reduce a total of 3 failing levels
	Mirror Individual
Where others would be broken by the weight of the world, you have created a procedure for dealing with hardship and pain. Your mind is your shelter and retreat where any and all grief can be processed in safety. While time may heal all eventually, you prefer to stare reality directly in the eye, judge yourself for what you did and did not do and repent when you know you were at fault.


[+] For every month you spend meditating on your failings, you may reduce the failing by an additional level
[-] Your convictions's roll bonuses are reduced by the ranks of failings attached to them
	• PSY 1
• get rid of all failings you have 3 times
	Non-Deterministic Truth Projector
Talking to you can often feel like playing two truths and a lie. You arrange your words in a way as to never quite conform to a point, leaving yourself ample space for plausible deniability and the manufacture of complete and utter falsehood. Your friends have gotten used to this and quickly shut you down when they spot it, but less familiar individuals may struggle to tell the difference between the real world and the one you conjured up.


[+] While performing another social roll you may make a CL 18 Deception check and add +2 to the original roll on success
[-] Failing this Deception check results in a -4 penalty to the original roll
	• PSY 2
• have spent 3 destiny points on aiding deception checks
	________________




Psyche Aspects
	Requirements
	Knower of Apparently Everyone
You are the first in line to meet and spend time with random people whenever you wander into a new place. Whenever you or one of your friends inevitably require an item, a service or information, you are there pointing them towards your recently acquired and sibling-like friend. While this sometimes gets exhausting, you are addicted to the satisfaction you feel from witnessing yet another of your socially stunted companions balk at you for having made connections so quickly.


[+] Once per month, you may retroactively declare you know of a person who could reasonably help with any given request.
[-] You must spend at least a week on socialization every month or suffer a crisis
	• PSY 2
• have made 3 acquaintances from strangers in unfamiliar places
	

	• PSY 2
•
	

