Equipment
Split into various miscellaneous categories, this section covers various pieces of equipment ranging from types of munitions and projectiles to various traps and constructs

Ammo
Ammo acts as a measure of how many times a ranged weapon can be used before it has to be reloaded. If the weapon does not have a defined ammo value, it can either be shot without reloading like a bow or it is not a ranged weapon. Reverie does not typically keep track of specific ammo counts, but exceptions could be made for specific narrative moments where ammo count could make a big difference. The only ammo that needs to be kept track of are the specialized arrows, bolts and munitions that offer additional effects.


