Concoctions
Concoctions can be a useful tool for adventurers who venture far from civilization or need a simple way to ensure a chance of recovery after being wounded. Their creation requires the necessary ingredients and a Medicine check with a CL equal to the number of ingredients +1. Ingredients are split into broad categories in order to ease their mechanical weight on the players.


Ingredients
	Name
	Found
	Value
	Basic Ingredients (BI)
	Anywhere in nature
	5
	Herbs
	Specific biomes
	20
	Excretions
	Animals
	40
	Toxins
	Venomous flora and fauna
	40
	Applicants
	Exotic plants
	60
	

Brewing
To brew a concoction, a character requires the necessary ingredients, a source of heat, some basic equipment like vials and a bit of time. Simple concoctions can be brewed over a period of 1h and can conveniently be made (and usually applied) during any kind of small rest. Other concoctions are brewed over a period of 4 hours and are to be planned for in advance of being needed.
To actually brew a concoction once everything is ready, the character makes a Medicine check with a CL dependent on the concoction being brewed. Multiple concoctions can be brewed at the same time provided there is required equipment and the CL of the check increases by 1 for each additional concoction. If the check results in a success, the character successfully makes 2 doses of the concoction, while they only make 1 dose on a failed check.
________________
Simple Concoctions
These are the most basic of concoctions and they require simple and common ingredients. They are a valuable addition to any party and their simplicity and affordability allow them to be frequently used.


